 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "freezer keeps beeping"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is the door being left open or a heavy load of food. Run your fingers round the rubber seal on the door and look for splits, gaps or a section that has come away, especially where the frost is. Is the seal torn or come away, was it dirty or folded (and is that sorted), or does it look fine?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "seal looks fine to me. no idea about frost, didn't look"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Check nothing is stopping the door — a shelf, drawer, bottle or food sticking out — and that the door hasn't dropped or gone loose on its hinge. Most fridge freezers also need the front feet raised slightly so the doors swing shut on their own. Was something in the way or it not standing right (and have you sorted it), is the hinge broken or the door dropped, or does the door shut and line up fine?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "the bottom freezer drawer wasn't pushed in properly last night, a bag was sticking out. i've shut it now"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: door not closing (loading / levelling)]\nGood news, that has sorted it. If it happens again, start with the same check. Is there anything else I can help with?\n[Panel: \"To check a suitable replacement — Enter your model number below. Once we have the model I can check whether a suitable replacement is available. It's usually on a sticker inside the door or around the frame, or on the back of the appliance.\"]"
  }
 ],
